// Under the parity law two origins add like waves: where both echoes land, they cancel.
name Interference
rule B1357/S1357
steps 3
hint Under this law two origins add like waves. Where both echoes land, they cancel out.
tip Two echoes, four cells apart. The centre column is where they cancelled each other out.
intro Two echoes crossed here. Where both arrived they cancelled, as waves do.
outro Where two things agree completely they leave nothing. You are learning the grammar.
